module test.claim.tailscale_join_fleet_membership_witness

// THE WITNESSES FOR "JOINED IS NOT THE SAME AS BEING THE FLEET'S" (2026-11-18).
//
// WHAT WAS FIXED. `extdeps.tailscale.join::tailscale_up_join_state_of` decided the join from
// `BackendState == "Running"` alone, and `gunbc.tailscale_join_converge` mapped that single joined arm to
// JoinPlanNoop first and unconditionally. A node Running on the tailnet WITHOUT the fleet's tag -- hand-joined
// under a personal account, or owned by a user -- was therefore reported CONVERGED while it sits outside every
// grant the fleet's tailnet policy is keyed on. The state is now three-valued at that boundary
// (extdeps.tailscale.join: WHETHER A HOST IS JOINED -- AND UNDER WHICH IDENTITY carries the ownership model and
// its upstream citations), and the middle state cannot be a Noop.
//
// WHY FIXTURES AND NOT LIVE READS. No live dispatch and no host read is in scope here, so the documents are
// fixtures under dag/test/fixture. Their SHAPE is upstream's -- `ipnstate.Status` members `BackendState`, `Self`,
// and `Self.Tags`, the last marked `json:",omitempty"`, which is how upstream spells a node with NO tags
// (ipn/ipnstate/ipnstate.go). The ken-shaped one carries what the specimen actually reported: Running, MagicDNS
// suffix tailecbe08.ts.net, DNSName ken.tailecbe08.ts.net., NO tags (operator_host_e2d4b7, read 2026-11-18 by
// still-fox-404). The identity members of the OTHER documents -- node ID, IPs -- are authored placeholders;
// nothing here is offered as a read of a live node, and `w_the_hand_joined_fixture_really_carries_no_tag_member`
// is what keeps the specimen fixture from being quietly re-tagged out of usefulness.
//
// WHICH FIXTURES ARE OBSERVATIONS AND WHICH ARE SHAPES. `tailscale_status_hand_joined_no_tags.json` transcribes
// the ken specimen as read. `tailscale_status_foreign_tag_only.json` is the dusk-1 shape -- a tailnet member that
// carries a DIFFERENT role's tag, recorded in extdeps.tailscale.acl beside dusk_serving_ip ("It is an untagged
// member device, so no tag grant reaches it"). The remaining three are authored shapes of states the fleet
// expects: a node enrolled by the fleet's tagged key, a logged-out node, and a document that cannot answer.
//
// THE RED THIS SET EXISTS TO BE. `w_the_specimen_refuses_typed_rather_than_noopping`,
// `w_noop_has_exactly_one_join_state_that_qualifies`, `w_a_fleet_member_still_noops_without_reading_the_key` and
// `w_the_refusal_outcome_never_settles_and_says_what_to_do` all go red the moment the fleet-tag check is removed
// from `tailscale_up_join_state_of`: with the check gone both tagless documents read as plain "joined", the plan
// arm becomes JoinPlanNoop, and each of those matches fails. That control was run on the branch (the run and its
// output are recorded in the PR), which is what DESIGN.md asks of a behavior fix: a witness that goes red when
// the behavior is wrong.
//


